Overlay patch 0044 (D29): OPENGL BACKEND GUARD -- never accept a renderer
this build does not compile.

WHY. LUS's Fast3dWindow constructor advertised FAST3D_SDL_OPENGL
unconditionally, but the iOS build of libultraship has no ENABLE_OPENGL (the
`if(IOS)` branch of libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt omits it; no
GfxRenderingAPIOGL in the binary). So a saved `Window.Backend.Id` = 2
("OpenGL") passed the availability check, InitWindowManager fell to
`default:` with null mWindowManagerApi/mRenderingApi, and Interpreter::Init
segfaulted before any log line: an unrecoverable launch crash. The game's own
Settings > Renderer API combobox listed "OpenGL" for the same reason, so one
tap bricked the app until reinstall. Found in 2ship2harkinian-ios OTA 1.1.1.1
(2026-10-09). Newer LUS pins (Ghostship, PaperBoat) already wrap the call in
#ifdef ENABLE_OPENGL; this backports that and adds two belts.

WHAT (src Fast3dWindow.cpp only):
  1. AddAvailableWindowBackend(FAST3D_SDL_OPENGL) under #ifdef ENABLE_OPENGL
     (desktop/oracle builds define it and are unchanged).
  2. InitWindowManager `default:` -- after the upstream SPDLOG_ERROR, Apple
     builds select and construct the Metal pair instead of leaving nulls.
  3. One INFO line when the saved backend id is rejected:
     "Window backend: saved id X is not available in this build; using id Y".
     The config is then re-saved with the chosen backend (SetWindowBackend),
     so a poisoned json heals on the first launch.

Idempotent: if the edits are already applied the generator reverses them
first, so it runs against a vendor tree with or without 0044 applied. Every
edit asserts exactly one match.

--- a/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/Fast3dWindow.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/Fast3dWindow.cpp
@@ -33,7 +33,12 @@
         AddAvailableWindowBackend(Ship::WindowBackend::FAST3D_SDL_METAL);
     }
 #endif
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0044): advertise OpenGL only when it is compiled in. The
+    // iOS libultraship has no ENABLE_OPENGL; a saved/selected "OpenGL" used to
+    // leave a null renderer -> launch crash. Newer LUS guards it the same way.
+#ifdef ENABLE_OPENGL
     AddAvailableWindowBackend(Ship::WindowBackend::FAST3D_SDL_OPENGL);
+#endif
 }
 
 Fast3dWindow::Fast3dWindow(std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Ship::GuiWindow>> guiWindows)
@@ -123,7 +128,13 @@
 }
 
 void Fast3dWindow::InitWindowManager() {
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0044): log a rejected saved backend id (saved -> chosen).
+    const int savedBackendId = Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetConfig()->GetInt("Window.Backend.Id", -1);
     SetWindowBackend(Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetConfig()->GetWindowBackend());
+    if (savedBackendId != -1 && savedBackendId != static_cast<int>(GetWindowBackend())) {
+        SPDLOG_INFO("Window backend: saved id {} is not available in this build; using id {}", savedBackendId,
+                    static_cast<int>(GetWindowBackend()));
+    }
 
     switch (GetWindowBackend()) {
 #ifdef ENABLE_DX11
@@ -146,6 +157,15 @@
 #endif
         default:
             SPDLOG_ERROR("Could not load the correct rendering backend");
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+            // SOH_IOS (overlay 0044): never leave the renderer null (Interpreter::Init
+            // would segfault before any log). Apple builds always carry Metal.
+            SPDLOG_ERROR("Window backend id {} has no renderer in this build; falling back to Metal",
+                         static_cast<int>(GetWindowBackend()));
+            SetWindowBackend(Ship::WindowBackend::FAST3D_SDL_METAL);
+            mRenderingApi = new GfxRenderingAPIMetal();
+            mWindowManagerApi = new GfxWindowBackendSDL2();
+#endif
             break;
     }
 }
